peridot: adapt RPMh and touch drivers to the live peridot.dts

Audited bsd/dev/peridot_rpmh.c and bsd/dev/peridot_touch.c against
the FDT shipped with the device boot chain
(mu-build Resources/DTBs/peridot.dts) and PORTING.md. Two drivers
still carried sweet (SM7150) MMIO addresses verbatim from the
ios-sweet reference patches:

- RPMh: RH_RSC_PA/RH_TCS_PA were 0x18220000/0x18220d00 (a value
  present nowhere in peridot.dts). The DT has apps_rsc@17a00000
  with positional reg drv-0/1/2 (0x17a00000/0x17a10000/0x17a20000)
  and drv@2 qcom,tcs-offset 0xd00 -> active TCS 0x17a20d00.
  RH_DRV=2 matches the DT drv@2 that owns the pmxr2230 touch rails.
  Resource names: the DT supplies for xiaomi_touch are
  avdd-supply=ldob13 (pmxr2230 L13, fixed 3.3 V) and
  vdd-supply=ldob23 (pmxr2230 L23, fixed 1.8 V), both under
  rsc@17a00000/drv@2. peridot_rpmh_vreg_enable now accepts exactly
  these two names; cmd-db lookup by name was already dynamic.

- Touch: TOUCH_SE_PA was 0x00a84000 (spi@a84000 = ir-spi@0 in
  peridot.dts). xiaomi_touch@0 sits on spi@a90000 = GENI SE4,
  interrupt 0x165, interrupt-parent 0x16b = pinctrl@f000000,
  goodix,reset-gpio <0x16b 0x80>, goodix,irq-gpio <0x16b 0x81>.
  The driver now maps SE4 at 0xA90000 and TLMM at 0x0F000000 with
  only the two DT pins (128 reset, 129 IRQ). sweet-only pads
  (qup11 GPIO 6/7, VDD90 GPIO 90) and the wrapper1/SE7 GCC clock
  vote are removed: those GCC offsets are a sweet layout, unverified
  on SM8635 cliffs, and writing them could corrupt an unrelated
  clock. SE4 clocks are relied on being ABL-loaded per the driver's
  own contract ("Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware"), and the
  boot log records that choice.

- Log strings: "SE7"->"SE4", "L11C"->rail names, panel size
  1080x2400->1220x2712 (peridot.dts panel and PORTING.md).

- PeridotFramebuffer.cpp comments: the ABL splash and real panel are
  1220x2712 (fWidth/fHeight come from PE_current_console at runtime;
  present() already centers the 1125x2436 logical surface on the
  larger panel and crops the edges). Only the stale sweet-panel
  comments are updated; no behavioural change.

Evidence: peridot.dts rsc@17a00000 (line 6320), spi@a90000
(line 16406), pinctrl@f000000 phandle 0x16b, rpmh-regulator-ldob13/
ldob23 (lines 6875/7042, supplies of xiaomi_touch@0); PORTING.md
"rsc 0x17A00000, TCS 0x17A20D00", "GENI SE4 0xA90000", "TLMM
128 reset / 129 IRQ", "rails pmxr2230 ldob13 3.3V/ldob23 1.8V".

